WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
Bionic Commando, a new breed of hero.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:26.040
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.160
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.140
I'm Joe. And I'm Sam.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.660
And we have a full house today for a very important episode, guys.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:37.360
Finally, the long-awaited sequel to Commando.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.320
Woo! The reaction.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.600
Nobody cares, apparently.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:45.860
Did you guys...

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:47.260
Is this a sequel?

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.120
First off, is this a sequel to Commando?

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.000
They're both Capcom games.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.380
It was... I guess...

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:58.120
I guess technically it's a sequel, but it feels more like just like another story in the same

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.380
world. But I mean, it is later in that world.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:01.760
Is it in the same world?

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:02.940
Like, I didn't know that.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:03.740
It is.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.320
But isn't it like retroactively in the same world?

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:11.660
Yes. Because the only thing that implies to me that they're in the same world, maybe there is something

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:14.380
in the story, but the only thing that implies to me that they're in the same world is that

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:15.420
they're the same character.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.600
It's that Super Joe guy again.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.080
Oh, yes.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.240
Super Joe. Not to be confused with our Joe.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:25.540
Right. Well, I'm far from super.

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:26.980
He's a pretty good Joe.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.820
Yeah, I'm decent Joe.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.000
I'm actually trying to remember.

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:34.800
In Commando, that was a pretty like...

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.860
It was presenting itself as like, this is the real world, right?

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.440
Yes. World War II.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:44.000
Okay. So now Bionic Commando is, I guess, the alternate future.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:45.640
Yes, actually, right?

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:47.480
I mean...

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.420
Yeah, I guess...

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.240
No, it is. It's gotta be an alternate future.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:53.540
Let's get right into it because it's like they're not calling them Nazis, right?

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.740
They are like...

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:56.900
They are pretty much Nazis without the word.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:01:58.440
They were supposed to be though.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.900
Yes, they were supposed to be.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:04.440
And I think in the Japanese version, they do just outright call them Nazis.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:09.660
But I guess censorship things don't allow for that here in the States, even though

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:14.400
that's weird because we've definitely played World War II games where you fight all the

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.120
different axis powers.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.440
I think that was a Nintendo thing.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.100
Okay. Gotcha.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:22.300
Yeah. So maybe Nintendo was like, slow down there, buddy.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.920
Like, you can't call them Nazis, but you can definitely show Hitler's face exploding

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:29.760
at a certain point in this game.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:33.300
As long as you don't call him Hitler.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:34.940
Yeah. Hiltr.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:36.720
Yeah. Well, that's right.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.380
Right. So Joe, you mentioned they're called the bads, right?

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:40.560
That's not very intimidating.

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:44.200
I mean, what can be more intimidating than the bads?

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.340
They're bad. I mean, that's a great point.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.840
Thank you. Case closed.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:50.540
You've obviously argued before.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:57.300
I'm rather unprepared now to make my statement against the bads, but also like the general's

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.320
name is weird too, right?

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.200
Isn't it like General... General Isamo something or other?

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.340
Yeah. Lisa Moe Kilt.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:04.920
Yeah. So, um...

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.420
He's Scottish. He's not very intimidating there either.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:10.160
Yeah. He's Scottish. He runs a Nazi-like empire.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:17.240
And it's up to Super Joe, who must be just finishing his story in Commando and then saying

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.600
like, you know, I'm up to the task.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.360
I just took on an entire army.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.240
I'll do it again all by myself.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.680
But I thought that Super Joe was like, captured.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:33.920
I'm not very good at like, reading into this game, but aren't you trying to save Super Joe?

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.600
Yeah, I think... No, I think you got it.

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:38.160
He went in to do this and he fell.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:41.200
He was captured. So now you're sent in now after him.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.200
Yeah, our job is just to get Super Joe back.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:49.500
Because you'll remember, Sean, that Super Joe in Commando never had a bionic arm.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:53.600
Well, we don't know how, like, what happens after Commando.

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:57.620
Like, you could have gotten to like, a lawnmower accident or something along those lines.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:59.720
That's true. We need a Gaiden game.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:02.420
Yeah, yeah. We need to find out what happens in the in-between.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:03.980
That's actually what the anime covers.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.100
So you don't have to worry.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:06.940
Great. Yeah.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.400
So let's talk a little bit about Bionic Commando here.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:10.540
It's an action platformer.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:12.240
That's what I'm going to call it.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:17.440
I'm going to say platformer because you're definitely dealing with platforms here, even if you don't jump.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.100
Nobody said jumping was part of a platformer.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:24.900
I mean, I'm sure people have said it, but we haven't explicitly said it before.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:32.680
Got it. I don't think Shigeru Miyamoto, the guy who created platformers, would argue that Bionic Commando is not a platformer.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:35.560
And since I'm speaking for him, I speak with complete authority.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.240
Yeah. So say we all.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:40.080
And Super Joe, not Super Joe, sorry.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:42.460
You play this guy named Spencer, I think, right?

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:44.880
Spencer. Or maybe you go unnamed.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:45.920
Maybe you go unnamed.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:48.320
I thought he had a name, but it was something.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:49.720
I forgot. It was like Rad something.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:53.100
Maybe it's Spencer in the arcade game, which is slightly different.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.260
So we're not counting that here.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:05:02.520
Anyway, the player you are is equipped with a Bionic Arm that has like a, it's like a grapple of sorts.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:07.280
And it allows him to pull himself forward or, you know, diagonally.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.300
So this way he can swing from the platforms.

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:11.320
So there's no jumping whatsoever.

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:13.260
Everything is done through this arm.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:21.280
And then also, in the other hand, I guess you have your gun, which allows you to shoot at enemies and use other various power ups.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:26.080
But, you know, to say that that's the game is kind of unfair, right?

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:27.480
I mean, there's so much to this game.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:32.740
I mean, just being, just focusing on that, though.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:36.420
Like that being the mechanic of like, you don't jump.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:41.140
You have this arm with the grappling and that's how you get around.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:50.640
And it, it, the programming of the game allows you to take advantage of that fact in a lot of different situations.

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:59.740
Like it's probably the most innovative game mechanic in platforming that we've seen since Super Mario Brothers.

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:08.780
Absolutely. I mean, nobody's going to argue here that, you know, the game is more notable today because of this feature of like not being able to jump.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.400
Because you have to use the arm for everything.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:13.160
That's what makes it a more notable NES title.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:17.740
And, and yeah, there's some flaws to the claw, but.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:20.000
Flaws to the claws.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:25.180
But for the most part, like that's what makes the game interesting.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:26.380
So let's talk about that.

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:28.760
A platform game in which you cannot jump.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.780
You know, Sean, you, you kind of started us already.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:34.240
So Joe, what were you, what were your immediate takes on that?

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:37.480
Well, right away, I was very excited about it.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:38.800
I thought it was a really cool idea.

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:48.480
And it's really, I don't know, just interesting to, to have a game that's kind of built like any other platformer we've, we've, you know, we've played with this claw in mind.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:52.840
But yeah, it has a different main mechanic than jumping to the platforms.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:56.080
And, you know, swinging in games is always fun.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:08.400
So it's an, it's an interesting thing where it, I feel like it had potential to be a little puzzly and potential to be a little, I don't know, like the, the action element of it being very cool.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:12.700
Um, and it delivered that to me for the most part.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:15.300
There definitely had things that it didn't deliver that I was hoping for.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:20.100
Um, but it, it definitely, you know, it scratched that itch for something new and something a little different.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:21.200
And Sam, what about you?

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:22.580
I thought it was great.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:40.720
I thought that the, the, the feel of it holds up and that the, like, I could tell when I started that when I was bad off, you know, at the very beginning, first time playing, it was just me not used to the controls yet, but that the controls themselves were very responsive.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:50.720
And I, you know, I looked up speed runs of this and people are just flying all over the place and it's something that you can get a lot better, uh, with, with time.

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:53.960
And so I think that that's a sign of a really good mechanic.

00:07:53.960 --> 00:08:11.500
Now we, we argued on the bubble bobble episode that, uh, in that game, there were too many differences on platforms of like, it's hard to know which ones you can just like jump right through and clip and which ones you're locked out of and which ones you can, um, you know, escape from.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:19.940
Did you guys have that same problem here in Bionic Commando of like platform differences of which ones you can, uh, just shoot upwards and climb up over?

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:21.980
Or for the most part, that was pretty clear.

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:33.800
It wasn't clear immediately, but it like, you learn pretty, pretty quickly that, uh, and the textures for these platforms are different enough that you, you get it.

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:39.060
Yeah. I think I remember like a couple of, a couple of instances where I was like, wait, I can't jump on this platform or what?

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:45.360
But like, for the most part, they were few enough and far enough between that, uh, it didn't really stand out as a major flaw to me.

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:59.780
I was going to say the springs kind of stand out a little bit too, not stand out and that they don't, they stand out and that they don't stand out and you jump, uh, when you hit them, which kind of surprises me every now and then when I step on them by accident.

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:16.920
I think the game also benefits a lot from being more open than Bubble Bobble was allowed to be, but also just from the fact that like you can, you can take the time to think about, you know, like what you want to, where you want to explore in this world and, uh, what you want to do in each level.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:21.380
There's no, uh, there's no instantly respawning enemies that you have to constantly deal with.

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:28.480
If you stay there too long, there's no, um, you know, there's no platforms that aren't communicated in a way where it's like, well, I can't reach that.

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:29.860
And I don't really know what to do next.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:35.620
You know, it's, you figure it out as you go along and it's not, it's not so puzzly in a way that's, um, obtuse.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:49.520
Uh, there's, there are some times in this game where depending on how you venture, uh, throughout the overworld in the different areas, you might be confused on what you're supposed to do next, but there, there is a solve for that that I think we'll get to.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:53.020
Did anybody have any problems though with using the hook?

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:56.180
I, I, I would just like to, uh, stop you real quick.

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:58.240
Um, I would just like some clarification.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:09:59.700
This is not a challenge.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:05.980
Um, but where did we get to like the comparison for this game is bubble bobble.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:09.340
Is it because it's sort of like, it's, it's kind of physics based.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:11.060
Is that what we're talking about here?

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:24.820
We're talking just about the platforming and you know, sometimes in, um, sometimes in Bionic Commando, there are platforms that you can reach up to, but you can't climb up on top of like they're, they're just solid walls.

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:32.520
Okay. And that was a thing in bubble bobble that we like, sometimes we couldn't escape walls or we couldn't go through those walls.

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:35.100
Like we had to, uh, find creative solutions.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:44.460
And I was just wondering if people had that same problem here because that's a, you know, that's just a platformer thing is like you have to be able to explore the area freely.

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:55.400
No, for sure. But to answer your actual question regarding if I had any problems with the grapple, um, there's definitely a learning curve, uh, where,

00:10:55.400 --> 00:11:00.700
in the beginning you, you really aren't sure how it works at all.

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:03.820
Uh, that lasts about like a minute and a half.

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:10.820
And then there's like, you kind of get the whole swinging mechanic and that lasts a couple hours.

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:20.160
And then you get to a point where you can start to like string these swings together and like get to places that you otherwise didn't think you could.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:22.480
And, but no, I mean there, there's dart.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:32.560
It's not a perfect system, but I, and I did have some issues with it throughout, but I otherwise thought that it's a pretty, uh, well polished system.

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:38.600
Yeah. I can, I can add to that a little bit too, because I agree that I don't think it's, it's a perfect system.

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:48.560
Um, and I, I, I agree that you can, that you learn, um, that you learn as you go and it does, you know, you, you do get a lot better at it.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:52.680
But I don't think that necessarily means that it's a good, that it's a well executed mechanic.

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:58.920
I think that there are, to me, I mean, personally, I thought there were some, some significant flaws in like the way it controlled.

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:12.980
Like one just being like, it's very counterintuitive that like the button to let go is like sometimes down and then, or to the left, whereas the button to grab on is a, and I feel like it sounds like, like a little thing.

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:19.740
But I feel like sometimes that, that makes like the, the fluidness of like the way you want to control, like a little more, a little more annoying.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:21.860
And granted, yeah, you get the hang of that after a while.

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:31.700
But then there are other things to me where if you swing and you're like just a little too close, just like a couple pixels too close to a wall, you'll bump into the wall and just fall straight down.

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:33.180
It'll, it'll stop all your momentum.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:35.760
Yeah. That's definitely one of the frustrations I meant.

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:42.400
Yeah. And it's, and there are a couple other things like that, that made this thing that I was really excited about at first.

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:52.540
That should have felt very fluid and very fun and like kind of the motion should have, it should have been very momentum based to use a term we've used in the past.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:56.380
And I feel like there was a lot of like stiffness to it.

00:12:57.480 --> 00:13:05.200
I'm just playing the devil's advocate a little bit here because I did still really like the mechanic, but I thought I would like to see it vastly improved.

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:10.920
I think part of that is there's no like aftertouch.

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:19.300
Like we're used to in midair being able to adjust our trajectory a la Super Mario.

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:26.960
But once you let go of that grapple or whatever the grapple was holding on to, you have committed to an arc.

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:37.980
Like, and that, like just that not being able to like make those little corrections definitely contributes to making that mechanic feel a bit stiff.

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:46.560
And the other, other aspects to it also contribute to that, that I guess I can't really articulate right now.

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:48.540
But I agree that there is a stiffness to it.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:53.940
But I do think that it, I was, I never really had trouble letting go.

00:13:55.300 --> 00:13:59.860
Or those, those binary things I didn't have as much issue with.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:04.760
Yeah, I mean, I don't think I was ever like looked at one of those things and was like, yeah, this is exactly what's giving me a problem.

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:08.580
But it was all the things compounded, which just made it feel not as fluid as it.

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:11.400
Like, I'm not asking for like Insomniac Spider-Man or anything.

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:16.440
But, you know, I just feel like the game being as action based as it is.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:26.440
Yeah. I feel like it should either have gone with keeping, with changing, making the controls a little more fluid to accommodate some of the action or keeping the controls the way they are.

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:31.300
But then making like the traversal a little more like of a cerebral puzzle.

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:35.460
But it kind of combined the wrong ends of both of those things together.

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:43.480
Because these, these constant, you know, like movements with the claw or arm, whatever grapple clip, whatever you want to call it.

00:14:44.140 --> 00:14:47.960
Those constant decisions you have to make with it do slow down the pace of the game.

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:55.060
And I'm not sure if that's a good or bad thing because I don't think this is a game that you're supposed to beat very quickly.

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:58.200
It's a very long, difficult, detailed game.

00:14:58.200 --> 00:15:04.720
But all that said, and this is going to sound crazy to suggest for a game as notable as Bionic Commando.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:10.160
But if you remove the grappling hook, I mean, this is, you know, and you were able to jump.

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:18.200
Like, this is still a long, difficult, detailed game that would be enjoyable to play if you did have full control over your body.

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:22.140
That's an interesting way to phrase it.

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:23.840
If you had full control over your body.

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:27.800
Instead of being forced to climb onto things and swing.

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:36.980
I understand. I think that if it was jumping in addition to the grapple, I guess I wouldn't, I wouldn't really know how they'd map that.

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:43.360
But I think that it would definitely contribute to a little bit of a better, like, game feel.

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:53.360
But I also just think that that is kind of, that is kind of like sacrilege to say the Bionic Commando, like, without the Bionic Arm.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:57.840
I guess I really don't have anything to say beyond that.

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:10.720
Just those musings. When I'm taking what you're saying, the way I'm taking what you're saying, Mike, is that, like, it has a lot of the features that we praise in other games that don't have this cool, interesting, new way of playing it.

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:15.380
Like, there are multiple, you know, there's a little bit of freedom in where you choose to go.

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:18.520
And there's, like, a lot of different items and power-ups you can use.

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:24.060
There's a lot of other things that you can, it's a very immersive game regardless of that mechanic.

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:31.240
Yeah, and I think that the arm, while being, like, restrictive, is used appropriately and makes the game more interesting.

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:35.420
Like, you would definitely have to change some design decisions if you incorporated jumping.

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:40.560
I'm just not so certain that I would hate the version of this game where you are able to jump.

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:49.900
You know, like, I feel like I would feel, and, you know, maybe this is just me not willing to put up with the slow pace of this game because of the claw.

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:55.500
But I feel like I would enjoy this game more if I was able to jump and freely explore in that manner.

00:16:55.800 --> 00:17:02.240
Now, Sean, you mentioned that, like, maybe there's a way where you still have the claw but are able to jump.

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:06.260
And that's where I kind of thought that the grappling hook missed some features.

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:12.680
There should have been an ability to maybe, like, grab enemies and pull them towards you with the grappling hook.

00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:19.140
Or maybe, like, a pulley system where you are, you know, your arm is so much stronger than you so it plays up on the strength of it.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:26.400
And you're able to, like, grab onto things and change platform heights and weights or things like that with this bionic arm.

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:32.580
Maybe the claw itself gets some, like, powerful upgrades that then expand on areas you've already visited.

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:34.540
Now, that changes the game a little more than that.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:42.020
But you get the idea. Like, I felt like other than swinging and climbing up on platforms, which is a huge part of this game,

00:17:42.280 --> 00:17:45.260
if you incorporated the jumping, the claw could still find some uses.

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:49.760
Sure. I still don't really know.

00:17:50.240 --> 00:17:56.200
I know it sounds very silly, but I still don't know how they'd map that control if you're still going to shoot things.

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:58.680
But I do get what you mean.

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:01.920
I think, though, that just the...

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:03.560
And this is...

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:06.680
It's not based on the game by itself, but also its legacy.

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:13.000
But the legacy of this game would be so much different if, like, we just got rid of the claw.

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:15.320
I mean, that sounds very obvious, but...

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.380
No, totally. It would be a more forgettable game.

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:21.240
I think people remember this one because of this distinct mechanic.

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:22.760
And so...

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:24.680
It feels good to do most of the time.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:33.520
Yeah, totally. I think that it's a conversation worth having, though, of, is the game actually better for having this mechanic on a gameplay fun level,

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:36.860
as opposed to just, like, obviously, obviously it makes it stand out.

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:41.500
But I think it's also cool just because it forces you to think of things in a way...

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:48.800
If you could jump, even if you could jump and you had the claw, you would probably jump a lot and not use the claw a lot.

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:53.520
And this forces you to kind of learn something new and think of it in a way you wouldn't think of in another game.

00:18:53.520 --> 00:19:00.660
And that's why, again, to answer your question, Mike, would this still be fun?

00:19:00.800 --> 00:19:02.120
Maybe. But would it be as fun?

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:05.180
I don't think so. I think that the fun...

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:10.920
I probably would not be as engaged in the game if I didn't have the swinging claw.

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:12.560
Sam, anything additional?

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:15.720
I was going to say that pretty much the same thing.

00:19:15.860 --> 00:19:18.840
Like, you know, the claw is what makes the game the game.

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:20.700
I think that also...

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:27.700
A couple other things. The way that you find each location in the game and you kind of have to discover what's there,

00:19:27.780 --> 00:19:32.200
and then you need to make sure that you have enough fuel to get to the next location for that long stretch.

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:39.060
Um, I think that all of that kind of gives it a puzzle element that it makes those little sections...

00:19:39.980 --> 00:19:46.780
I mean, the fact that, like, enemies go down in a couple hits and that the sections themselves aren't super challenging,

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:51.260
but it's all part of this larger picture that you have to figure out and navigate.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:55.300
Almost like a Metroidvania, but not quite because it's still pretty linear.

00:19:56.060 --> 00:19:58.520
I think that that is, um...

00:19:58.520 --> 00:20:00.620
That is what makes it a really interesting game as well.

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:03.400
Um, and as far as the claw mechanic goes,

00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:08.560
I was wondering if maybe if you had, like, a little bit of, um...

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:12.280
Like, a little bit slower falling speed, if that would help things.

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:15.560
So that way you could kind of re-grab if you made a mistake or something.

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:17.780
Oh, without losing all progress.

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:18.780
Yeah, if you were fast enough.

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:20.060
.

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:51.540
Thank you.

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:29.540
That's cool. And, you know, I'm really glad that you brought up the larger picture of the game, too, because the way that we're treating the game, you know, it's almost like you complete stage one, you move on to stage two.

00:21:29.980 --> 00:21:42.440
And even though these stages aren't numbered appropriately, and I'm not quite sure what that's about, when you boot up the game, you're greeted with this, like, what are we going to call these things now?

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:43.900
It's like a map grid.

00:21:44.180 --> 00:21:45.980
Yeah. Like flow chart.

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:48.220
I don't know. Yeah, it's like a map flow chart.

00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:55.080
That's a good way of like you start on one and then you could move to 13, I think, or 14.

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:57.240
And then you could move from there to number three.

00:21:57.440 --> 00:21:59.340
It's like, why aren't they just numbered in order?

00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:00.480
I think I don't know.

00:22:00.480 --> 00:22:04.760
I think I know why. I think it's because you're not supposed to do them in order, you know?

00:22:04.900 --> 00:22:09.580
And if they were just numbered one through 14 or whatever, then you would just do it in that order.

00:22:09.740 --> 00:22:13.280
But this kind of makes you think about which one you should go to.

00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:17.020
And they'll say there's a weapons depot in sector four or something.

00:22:17.360 --> 00:22:19.180
And then you're like, all right, where is sector four?

00:22:19.240 --> 00:22:20.940
And how do I get there? And I have to go through all these.

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:22.680
I guess that's right.

00:22:22.740 --> 00:22:24.460
But there doesn't seem to be any rhyme or reason.

00:22:24.620 --> 00:22:25.560
Like, I understand that.

00:22:25.620 --> 00:22:32.380
Like, yes, it's sort of it's trying to train you to not think of them as level one, two, three, four, five.

00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:41.860
But neither the order in which you should play them nor the order in which they are presented are numbered correctly.

00:22:42.140 --> 00:22:45.420
So, I mean, it just it's still very confusing.

00:22:45.420 --> 00:22:52.100
And it is one of it is one of the reasons why I had trouble playing this game over like in the overview.

00:22:53.780 --> 00:22:55.460
Moment to moment, I was good.

00:22:55.600 --> 00:22:59.620
But this whole system here kind of threw me for a loop.

00:22:59.620 --> 00:23:07.600
I was going to say I was a little confused until I started using the radio or the transmission, whatever it is in the game a little bit more.

00:23:07.600 --> 00:23:13.520
I did that as well, yeah. And then it kind of gives you directions there and it tells you hints of places to go.

00:23:13.680 --> 00:23:17.500
And so I just kind of I don't really think too much about where I'm trying to go.

00:23:17.680 --> 00:23:20.440
I just kind of let the game play itself sort of.

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:23.780
Yeah, go where the hints guide you because I'd argue that they're not even hints.

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:25.960
They're essential to playing the game.

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:35.980
Yeah. Like if you if you don't do those transmissions, you won't even understand like why you can't go to area four until you get that like ability to see in the dark.

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:38.740
Yeah, that's also part of it, though.

00:23:38.940 --> 00:23:41.860
Like that whole like, oh, these are hints.

00:23:42.080 --> 00:23:45.680
These are things that tell you where you should go or where things are.

00:23:46.640 --> 00:23:49.400
But I didn't know why I needed that thing.

00:23:49.640 --> 00:23:55.180
Like I know I know that like, you know, area four is kind of impossible without that night vision thing.

00:23:55.380 --> 00:24:03.000
But like there was a point where I was trying to get to area eight and just said, like, you don't have enough power to do that.

00:24:03.340 --> 00:24:13.580
And I didn't recall any level or any radio station that told you that, like, to get enough power to go to level eight, you need this.

00:24:13.580 --> 00:24:15.200
I'm sure it exists somewhere.

00:24:16.040 --> 00:24:23.740
And if I played this game long enough, like a kid in 88 that didn't have many other games to play, I might figure that out.

00:24:23.900 --> 00:24:26.820
But it was still a little obtuse for me.

00:24:27.180 --> 00:24:29.640
Yeah, I also noticed like a couple of things like that.

00:24:29.800 --> 00:24:36.840
I don't know how I missed it telling me that I needed the light to go to area four.

00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:41.520
But I went to area four and then I was just, can you leave the area?

00:24:41.780 --> 00:24:43.420
I mean, you're just stuck in that area.

00:24:43.580 --> 00:24:49.460
Yeah. So, but then you die, do you, I'm forgetting, do you end up outside of, you end up back in the area when you die?

00:24:49.680 --> 00:24:51.800
Oh, you're right. You were just respawned.

00:24:51.820 --> 00:24:53.100
Yeah, you know, it's funny.

00:24:53.100 --> 00:24:54.120
I don't know what you would do.

00:24:54.620 --> 00:24:56.700
Yeah, I ended up, I was pretty early on.

00:24:56.800 --> 00:25:00.660
It was only like the second or third place I went to and I had to start the game over.

00:25:01.540 --> 00:25:03.080
Dang. So that sucked.

00:25:03.740 --> 00:25:06.740
So I don't know if maybe I missed some very simple solution to that.

00:25:06.900 --> 00:25:10.980
But if I didn't, that seems like a very major flaw in the game.

00:25:10.980 --> 00:25:16.560
And, you know, we're talking about being able to explore these areas freely and everything.

00:25:16.560 --> 00:25:19.560
And on the same map, you can go wherever you want.

00:25:19.680 --> 00:25:24.000
But the enemies on screen in these trucks also are able to go wherever they want.

00:25:24.200 --> 00:25:35.620
And there's almost like this, you know, early tactical strategy game going on there where you have to be mindful of where the trucks are so that you don't come into collision with them.

00:25:35.620 --> 00:25:39.360
Granted, the penalty for coming into collision with them isn't really that bad.

00:25:39.520 --> 00:25:43.500
It's almost like you get to enter a minigame of Commando.

00:25:43.800 --> 00:25:54.400
But I thought that was pretty cool of like a nice touch to, you know, to make the map flowchart thing we were talking about feel more alive than just like picking numbers on a square.

00:25:54.400 --> 00:25:57.780
No, it definitely felt cooler because of that.

00:25:58.340 --> 00:26:14.120
But, yeah, honestly, that minigame slash punishment is so, like, trivial because it really is just like the same, like, mini level of Commando over and over that, like, it may as well not have been there.

00:26:14.120 --> 00:26:22.720
But the feel of it being included did help just like, yeah, exactly what you said, made the map feel a bit more alive.

00:26:23.560 --> 00:26:25.460
Yeah, it helps with immersion, I think.

00:26:25.500 --> 00:26:31.320
These are actually convoys that are going about their business and you have come upon them.

00:26:31.440 --> 00:26:35.940
Right. And you can go into one of these levels and literally just run through it and not shoot anyone.

00:26:36.080 --> 00:26:37.300
Yeah. Just run past everyone and you're done.

00:26:38.460 --> 00:26:43.540
I also found that I look this game up online a lot to see what people think of it because I know it has a legacy.

00:26:45.220 --> 00:26:51.680
And people like those little mini levels because there's the guy that drops, I think it's the eagle symbol.

00:26:52.240 --> 00:26:54.220
And those are extra lives.

00:26:54.240 --> 00:27:01.560
And you can actually farm those guys to get a bunch of extra lives and then kind of set yourself up for later.

00:27:01.580 --> 00:27:12.780
Yeah, I guess I never really noticed that because your extra lives aren't all that easy to see.

00:27:12.880 --> 00:27:13.940
Yeah. At least.

00:27:14.640 --> 00:27:20.240
So I never really noticed that, but it sucks because farming should never really be a mechanic.

00:27:21.900 --> 00:27:22.840
But that's all.

00:27:22.840 --> 00:27:23.660
Well, wait a minute. Wait a minute.

00:27:23.760 --> 00:27:25.820
What about like farming and RPGs?

00:27:25.920 --> 00:27:27.880
Like that's like a whole element of those games.

00:27:27.880 --> 00:27:29.820
I think that farming and RPGs.

00:27:29.820 --> 00:27:30.780
We're getting off topic here.

00:27:30.860 --> 00:27:40.280
But I think that farming and RPGs is a symptom of like poor game design than it is until it became a mechanic in itself.

00:27:40.500 --> 00:27:43.280
I think it was a symptom of poor game design before it became a mechanic.

00:27:44.240 --> 00:27:53.660
You know, I agree with that too because there are definitely some RPGs where you don't have to ever stop and think about like I should stay in this area for a long time.

00:27:53.780 --> 00:27:55.640
Yeah. And just keep battling the same thing over and over.

00:27:55.740 --> 00:27:56.780
So I agree with that. Yeah, exactly.

00:27:56.780 --> 00:27:57.800
I retract my statement.

00:27:57.980 --> 00:28:00.080
You guys are making me think a lot tonight.

00:28:00.080 --> 00:28:07.960
I think when Sam brought up that thing about the numbers, that was just something I never considered in my whole life that they would number them out of orders.

00:28:08.020 --> 00:28:11.580
This way you don't think of them as something you must do in order.

00:28:11.740 --> 00:28:12.800
But that was such a good point.

00:28:13.120 --> 00:28:18.700
And so shout out to the nostalgia crew for making this nostalgia listener think differently.

00:28:20.060 --> 00:28:21.560
Thanks, man. All right.

00:28:21.640 --> 00:28:22.800
So, you know what, though? What?

00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:24.100
You know, we're talking about this game.

00:28:24.240 --> 00:28:27.300
And obviously, like this is one that we all put a lot of time into.

00:28:27.300 --> 00:28:34.200
Sometimes we're, you know, we're being honest with listeners and we're like, oh, I didn't really play this one that much or it wasn't that fun after a while.

00:28:34.300 --> 00:28:35.240
So I just gave up on it.

00:28:35.260 --> 00:28:36.780
But it sounds like we all really played this one.

00:28:37.280 --> 00:28:39.960
However, I doubt that any of us beat it.

00:28:40.140 --> 00:28:41.700
Am I correct? You're correct.

00:28:42.980 --> 00:28:47.700
This is a long game and that shouldn't be a penalty.

00:28:48.140 --> 00:28:52.140
But I'm starting to notice myself in this trend of NES games.

00:28:52.140 --> 00:28:57.640
Maybe even, you know, like outside of Legend of Zelda is the only like longish one.

00:28:57.800 --> 00:28:59.960
And that's not even that long of a game if we're being honest with ourselves.

00:29:00.180 --> 00:29:01.440
But that one lets you save.

00:29:01.600 --> 00:29:04.240
That's the only longish game that I actually was able to like tolerate.

00:29:04.480 --> 00:29:11.080
Any of these longer NES games, it seems like they're fine and they're interesting games and I'd still play them regardless.

00:29:11.240 --> 00:29:15.220
But I don't actually have an interest in beating them because of their length.

00:29:15.520 --> 00:29:16.360
Do you guys find that?

00:29:16.360 --> 00:29:22.920
I mean, I think that I agree as a 29-year-old.

00:29:23.620 --> 00:29:26.100
But I don't think that's an us problem.

00:29:26.240 --> 00:29:27.400
That is not the game's problem.

00:29:27.780 --> 00:29:37.100
Because with games like, I don't remember, the ones where it's basically the same thing over and over.

00:29:37.620 --> 00:29:39.320
There's no real progression.

00:29:39.620 --> 00:29:43.140
It's just like this game has 200 stages.

00:29:43.580 --> 00:29:45.240
Like that is too long.

00:29:45.240 --> 00:29:50.220
Like that is a game that I would not play because it's so long.

00:29:50.540 --> 00:29:55.440
But this is a relatively like progression-based game.

00:29:55.660 --> 00:29:59.420
So I don't really see that as a fault in the game.

00:29:59.540 --> 00:30:02.520
I think that's just our patience as people.

00:30:03.520 --> 00:30:05.040
Of which I have very little.

00:30:05.200 --> 00:30:11.240
So I agree with that. But I'd be curious to hear Sam and Joe's thoughts on just like completing NES games in general.

00:30:11.240 --> 00:30:16.040
Like does a longer NES game drive you away from it?

00:30:16.180 --> 00:30:17.600
Or do you not care about beating them?

00:30:17.760 --> 00:30:18.600
Like what's the deal?

00:30:18.680 --> 00:30:23.480
I think that the way that we play video games now is so different than the way people play video games in the 80s.

00:30:24.020 --> 00:30:28.820
That, you know, we're kind of used to the immediate gratification of getting it.

00:30:28.820 --> 00:30:33.720
Whereas back then you really had to fully understand the game for a while.

00:30:33.920 --> 00:30:37.520
And you probably weren't playing too many other games at home.

00:30:37.840 --> 00:30:40.140
So you had the time to do that too.

00:30:41.680 --> 00:30:48.380
And so, you know, maybe it does take a really long time before you can get to some of those later levels as a kid playing this game.

00:30:48.820 --> 00:30:52.100
But you put in so much time already because you don't really have that many options.

00:30:53.300 --> 00:30:56.080
That you have the swinging mechanic down.

00:30:56.580 --> 00:30:58.920
And you can just breeze through the beginning of it now.

00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:00.100
And you know exactly where to go.

00:31:00.220 --> 00:31:01.540
And you can kind of set yourself up.

00:31:01.760 --> 00:31:04.420
So I can see this like...

00:31:04.420 --> 00:31:06.520
And for that reason it really grows on you too.

00:31:07.500 --> 00:31:09.100
So I can forgive it for that.

00:31:09.100 --> 00:31:12.820
I think that if it came out today, then that would be a different story.

00:31:14.860 --> 00:31:17.940
But... If it came out today, it would have at least like an auto-save feature.

00:31:18.060 --> 00:31:20.020
Yeah. So I don't think it would have the same problem.

00:31:20.020 --> 00:31:22.420
Yeah, if there was an auto-save feature, I think that would be fine.

00:31:22.780 --> 00:31:24.180
But, you know. No, totally.

00:31:24.320 --> 00:31:25.500
And I think it's just like...

00:31:25.500 --> 00:31:27.380
It's something that we always think...

00:31:27.380 --> 00:31:28.460
Something I always think about.

00:31:28.560 --> 00:31:29.940
I don't want to say we all always think about.

00:31:30.020 --> 00:31:31.640
But it's something I'm always thinking about with these games.

00:31:31.780 --> 00:31:32.960
And just video games in general.

00:31:34.180 --> 00:31:37.400
Is my... My lack of care.

00:31:37.400 --> 00:31:40.160
I don't care of whether I beat games or not anymore.

00:31:40.620 --> 00:31:44.740
Like I really... Even modern games that are exciting, story-driven games.

00:31:45.060 --> 00:31:47.960
I'm okay with just like putting them down.

00:31:48.380 --> 00:31:49.340
When I've had enough.

00:31:49.420 --> 00:31:52.800
Yeah, I agree. Like I don't mind if I beat it or not.

00:31:53.020 --> 00:31:54.760
I can always look up the story on Wikipedia.

00:31:55.160 --> 00:31:56.120
I think...

00:31:56.120 --> 00:31:59.080
The guys on IGN GameScoop brought this up recently.

00:31:59.260 --> 00:32:00.360
But they were talking about like...

00:32:00.360 --> 00:32:02.800
That video games are the only medium.

00:32:02.900 --> 00:32:04.640
That you can't just like...

00:32:04.640 --> 00:32:06.800
Jump to the end and find out what happens.

00:32:06.900 --> 00:32:08.140
Like you can rent a movie.

00:32:08.400 --> 00:32:09.560
And just go on the DVD.

00:32:09.660 --> 00:32:10.740
And skip to the last chapter.

00:32:10.900 --> 00:32:11.880
And find out what happens.

00:32:11.940 --> 00:32:13.420
Or you can turn to the end of a book.

00:32:13.600 --> 00:32:16.260
And read the last page without like being skipped.

00:32:16.600 --> 00:32:19.200
In video games you don't have like necessarily...

00:32:19.200 --> 00:32:21.540
Some games give you chapter selects after the fact.

00:32:21.540 --> 00:32:23.400
But you don't get the ability to just like be like...

00:32:23.400 --> 00:32:24.520
I want to replay this moment.

00:32:24.520 --> 00:32:25.900
Because I really enjoyed it.

00:32:26.660 --> 00:32:28.220
I'm glad you brought that up Mike.

00:32:28.320 --> 00:32:29.880
Because I listened to that episode too.

00:32:30.040 --> 00:32:31.580
And I actually have like...

00:32:31.580 --> 00:32:33.140
It's weird because I have an opinion.

00:32:33.140 --> 00:32:35.640
That I don't think I really have a good way of defending.

00:32:36.300 --> 00:32:38.140
But I disagree with them.

00:32:39.080 --> 00:32:41.220
Even though like logically I agree with them.

00:32:41.720 --> 00:32:44.240
But I think that so much...

00:32:44.240 --> 00:32:45.540
Depending on the game.

00:32:45.860 --> 00:32:46.940
So like not every game.

00:32:47.120 --> 00:32:50.240
But like so much of a lot of like story-driven games.

00:32:50.240 --> 00:32:52.420
Or games that are for the experience.

00:32:53.520 --> 00:32:54.800
Like of the story.

00:32:56.840 --> 00:32:58.560
Part of it is that you're living it.

00:32:58.640 --> 00:32:59.700
That you're being rewarded.

00:32:59.940 --> 00:33:01.440
When you're getting whatever.

00:33:01.520 --> 00:33:03.220
The cutscene or whatever the next part of the story is.

00:33:03.280 --> 00:33:04.580
And that you're...

00:33:04.580 --> 00:33:06.760
You feel more immersed in it.

00:33:06.820 --> 00:33:07.860
Because you're...

00:33:07.860 --> 00:33:11.720
You know... You're the one with like some agency in it.

00:33:12.320 --> 00:33:14.360
And I totally get that.

00:33:14.780 --> 00:33:15.720
Like... Well yeah.

00:33:15.840 --> 00:33:18.160
But why shouldn't the person be able to decide...

00:33:18.160 --> 00:33:20.060
You know... You can make the same thing about a movie.

00:33:20.060 --> 00:33:21.160
Like you don't get as much out of it.

00:33:21.240 --> 00:33:22.440
If you skip to the end. But like yeah.

00:33:22.560 --> 00:33:24.300
The person who bought it should be allowed to do that.

00:33:24.580 --> 00:33:26.280
And I agree with that totally logically.

00:33:26.520 --> 00:33:28.520
But just somehow I don't like the idea of a world.

00:33:28.580 --> 00:33:29.740
Where all the games...

00:33:29.740 --> 00:33:31.620
You can just skip to the end if you want to.

00:33:32.360 --> 00:33:34.940
Yeah. With no real logical way of backing that up.

00:33:35.060 --> 00:33:36.100
This is a...

00:33:36.100 --> 00:33:39.020
This is a quagmire that we could step into.

00:33:39.200 --> 00:33:40.400
And talk for hours about.

00:33:41.920 --> 00:33:42.880
I... But no.

00:33:43.000 --> 00:33:44.420
I kind of see...

00:33:44.420 --> 00:33:46.180
I kind of see both camps of this.

00:33:46.180 --> 00:33:48.520
Where I think that...

00:33:48.520 --> 00:33:51.400
It's weird that you can't just go and look.

00:33:51.500 --> 00:33:52.660
But I wouldn't want to.

00:33:52.880 --> 00:33:54.780
So I've never really thought about that.

00:33:55.260 --> 00:33:56.980
I haven't listened to that episode.

00:33:57.580 --> 00:33:58.840
So maybe I should.

00:33:59.020 --> 00:34:04.000
Just to get a little bit more information on where they're coming from.

00:34:04.140 --> 00:34:05.920
But I just wouldn't want to.

00:34:05.920 --> 00:34:09.340
I have a very specific anecdotal counterpoint to this.

00:34:10.480 --> 00:34:16.100
That... Sure. When I was a kid I got a used copy of Ocarina of Time.

00:34:16.480 --> 00:34:18.500
And that person had already beaten the game.

00:34:18.740 --> 00:34:22.900
And so I was curious what it would be like to be in the end of the game.

00:34:24.060 --> 00:34:24.860
So me...

00:34:24.860 --> 00:34:27.060
You know. I was still a kid I think.

00:34:27.440 --> 00:34:28.440
You know. Like still Kid Link.

00:34:29.640 --> 00:34:32.480
And I just decided I'd play this other person's file for a little bit.

00:34:32.580 --> 00:34:33.960
And see what it would be like to fight Ganon.

00:34:35.080 --> 00:34:36.100
And it was cool.

00:34:36.140 --> 00:34:37.120
And I got really good at it.

00:34:37.200 --> 00:34:40.040
So by the time that I finally got there.

00:34:40.040 --> 00:34:41.220
I knew exactly what to do.

00:34:41.820 --> 00:34:45.000
And I don't know if that really like ruined the end of it for me or not.

00:34:45.100 --> 00:34:47.920
But I thought it was fun that I could go over to my friend's house.

00:34:47.960 --> 00:34:49.860
Who was having trouble beating Ganon.

00:34:49.940 --> 00:34:50.880
And I could do it for him.

00:34:51.300 --> 00:34:54.360
Whereas I'm still like in Jabu Jabu's belly.

00:34:54.820 --> 00:34:55.880
So. Yeah.

00:34:56.060 --> 00:34:57.180
I mean that's awesome to hear.

00:34:57.240 --> 00:34:58.700
I'm kind of surprised that you weren't like.

00:34:59.000 --> 00:34:59.940
What? Link's an adult?

00:35:00.140 --> 00:35:01.260
But maybe that was just spoiled.

00:35:01.340 --> 00:35:03.020
Because that's something that's obvious from like.

00:35:03.020 --> 00:35:06.760
Like anywhere. Any promotional material for Ocarina of Time.

00:35:07.160 --> 00:35:09.400
However. You know. Just to bring this back to my Ionic Commando.

00:35:09.560 --> 00:35:11.800
Because I didn't bring this up just to derail us from that.

00:35:11.980 --> 00:35:14.640
Is that. I was interested in this game.

00:35:14.740 --> 00:35:15.880
And I was having a good time with it.

00:35:15.900 --> 00:35:17.960
So I would have liked the ability to just like.

00:35:18.560 --> 00:35:20.420
You know. Whether it's through a cheat code or something.

00:35:20.640 --> 00:35:22.320
Like. Be able to just experience.

00:35:22.600 --> 00:35:24.020
Like. How this game ends.

00:35:24.140 --> 00:35:25.920
And stuff like that. Instead of having to go to YouTube.

00:35:26.380 --> 00:35:27.240
So. I don't know.

00:35:27.360 --> 00:35:28.320
Like. It just made me think of that.

00:35:28.320 --> 00:35:29.620
Like. It's a bit of a bummer.

00:35:29.740 --> 00:35:31.960
That I have to. Constantly replay.

00:35:32.720 --> 00:35:34.740
The. The beginnings of games.

00:35:35.080 --> 00:35:37.760
That I. You know. That I turned out knowing very well.

00:35:38.360 --> 00:35:39.720
But. When it comes to like.

00:35:39.780 --> 00:35:42.100
The end of games. It's something that I rarely experience.

00:35:42.980 --> 00:35:44.180
I think that this can.

00:35:44.360 --> 00:35:45.860
I mean. Maybe this isn't what you're saying.

00:35:46.020 --> 00:35:47.940
And I do get that you're talking about.

00:35:48.120 --> 00:35:49.140
Sort of like a chapter select.

00:35:49.280 --> 00:35:50.640
To some extent. But.

00:35:50.800 --> 00:35:53.240
I. I think that. My opinion is just like.

00:35:53.340 --> 00:35:54.740
Maybe this game should have had a save feature.

00:35:54.900 --> 00:35:55.760
Or a password feature.

00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:58.420
And that's. That's just where I would stop.

00:35:59.040 --> 00:36:00.320
Sure. I love that argument.

00:36:01.080 --> 00:36:02.800
Yeah. I would argue that.

00:36:03.100 --> 00:36:04.380
The fact that Nintendo.

00:36:04.880 --> 00:36:06.280
Introduced the ability to save.

00:36:06.400 --> 00:36:08.660
With Legend of Zelda. Led to like.

