00:44:59.840 --> 00:45:01.920
this one also falls into that category.

00:45:01.920 --> 00:45:05.560
So I'm going to slide it in there, and I'm not trying to take away from it and say,

00:45:05.760 --> 00:45:08.380
well, it just barely makes my essential games list.

00:45:08.480 --> 00:45:09.500
No, it's on there, you know?

00:45:09.660 --> 00:45:12.360
And I had a good time playing this, and I think at the very least,

00:45:12.600 --> 00:45:16.840
if you're a huge NES fan and you haven't played Bionic Commando yet,

00:45:17.320 --> 00:45:18.740
chances are you're going to like this one.

00:45:18.780 --> 00:45:24.120
Because I think, you know, the things that make Bionic Commando struggle a little bit

00:45:24.120 --> 00:45:28.160
could actually be fun to most fans of NES-style games.

00:45:28.160 --> 00:45:33.280
Like, this could be the challenge you've been looking for that other platformers didn't quite deliver on.

00:45:33.380 --> 00:45:34.740
So I'm going to put it on there.

00:45:35.000 --> 00:45:35.860
Sam, why don't you go next?

00:45:35.860 --> 00:45:41.620
Thanks, Joe. I think this is a great game.

00:45:41.760 --> 00:45:45.360
I love how you have to figure out what you're doing in each level

00:45:45.860 --> 00:45:47.520
