00:45:52.480 --> 00:45:55.200
but I know that this level is like this from the last time I played it,

00:45:55.360 --> 00:45:57.280
so I have to figure something out.

00:45:57.380 --> 00:46:02.380
It's a very thoughtful game in that the whole game is the puzzle.

00:46:03.440 --> 00:46:10.780
I think that the grappling hook, you know, the claw mechanic is really cool,

00:46:10.880 --> 00:46:12.080
and they do it well.

00:46:12.580 --> 00:46:14.900
And it kind of has that NES,

00:46:15.540 --> 00:46:17.740
I'm not going to say jank because it's not jank,

00:46:18.900 --> 00:46:21.820
just, like, you know, difficulty.

00:46:23.660 --> 00:46:25.220
But that, like you said,

00:46:25.300 --> 00:46:29.900
that's something that people who are a fan of this kind of NES games

00:46:29.900 --> 00:46:33.300
and that style of difficulty will really enjoy.

00:46:33.380 --> 00:46:36.120
And it's the kind of thing where you can get better and better at it.

00:46:36.940 --> 00:46:38.740
So I think it's essential.

00:46:38.740 --> 00:46:39.640
It's on my list.

00:46:39.840 --> 00:46:42.840
Very cool. So that's two, but we need majority.

00:46:43.420 --> 00:46:45.260
So, Sean, what do you say?

00:46:46.980 --> 00:46:49.480
So this is definitely a flawed game.

00:46:50.460 --> 00:46:53.480
We've kind of gone into great detail

00:46:53.480 --> 00:46:56.220
about all the things that would have made this game feel better,

00:46:57.940 --> 00:47:01.780
improvements that could have been made to the overworld,

00:47:01.780 --> 00:47:08.620
how, like, the interceptions by the trucks are kind of trivial

00:47:08.620 --> 00:47:10.020
and don't really matter,

00:47:10.840 --> 00:47:15.280
and how the claw sometimes doesn't feel quite right.

00:47:16.160 --> 00:47:20.140
But I think that those are all just on the periphery,

00:47:20.140 --> 00:47:23.600
and the core of the game is very fun.

00:47:23.620 --> 00:47:27.640
And I will sort of go against sort of what Mike said

00:47:27.640 --> 00:47:32.060
in that he didn't go so far as to say that it was innovative.

00:47:32.060 --> 00:47:34.680
I will say, and I already have said that it is innovative,

00:47:34.980 --> 00:47:39.320
this mechanic of, like, every other platformer

00:47:39.320 --> 00:47:43.380
is just jumping, either jump and jump or jump and shoot.

00:47:43.380 --> 00:47:45.500
This is shoot and claw.

00:47:45.780 --> 00:47:48.660
So I will say that it is innovative,

00:47:48.680 --> 00:47:49.860
I will say that it is fun,

00:47:49.940 --> 00:47:51.180
and I will say that it's essential.

00:47:51.440 --> 00:47:53.520
All right. So that puts it on the list,

00:47:53.520 --> 00:47:56.220
but, Joe, you can still have a say.

00:47:56.700 --> 00:47:58.660
As powerless as you feel right now,

00:47:58.880 --> 00:47:59.980
you still have something.

00:48:00.200 --> 00:48:02.000
I don't feel like super Joe right now.

00:48:02.060 --> 00:48:04.320
I feel like powerless Joe,

00:48:04.460 --> 00:48:06.800
but I'll give my opinion anyways.

00:48:07.180 --> 00:48:09.540
So I grappled with this, no pun intended,

00:48:09.740 --> 00:48:12.780
I grappled with this for a long time with this one.

00:48:13.760 --> 00:48:17.260
This one is, it gave me some trouble

00:48:17.260 --> 00:48:18.900
because I loved this game.

00:48:18.960 --> 00:48:20.200
I thought it was great.

00:48:20.680 --> 00:48:21.560
From beginning to end,

00:48:21.600 --> 00:48:23.400
I really do think that the claw thing

00:48:23.400 --> 00:48:27.800
is a very cool, interesting mechanic

00:48:27.800 --> 00:48:29.260
that makes you think differently,

00:48:29.260 --> 00:48:32.040
and I really want to make sure that we praise them

00:48:32.040 --> 00:48:35.780
for kind of branching out and trying something else.

00:48:36.000 --> 00:48:41.140
And there are a lot of things that made me question

00:48:41.140 --> 00:48:43.240
whether or not I wanted to put on the essential games list.

00:48:43.360 --> 00:48:44.460
Most of what we talked about,

00:48:44.540 --> 00:48:46.860
like the grappling hook,

00:48:47.540 --> 00:48:49.380
being their major main mechanic,

00:48:49.380 --> 00:48:51.520
not feeling quite good enough,

00:48:51.740 --> 00:48:53.860
feeling like it could really be improved on.

00:48:54.000 --> 00:48:55.480
And I would really love to see

00:48:55.480 --> 00:48:57.420
just like a direct sequel on the NES

00:48:58.080 --> 00:48:59.160
that improves on it.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:02.020
But then there's also some things like enemy placement,

00:49:02.200 --> 00:49:03.560
enemies respawn almost immediately.

00:49:04.220 --> 00:49:06.000
It's the same issue we've had with other things,

00:49:06.160 --> 00:49:08.760
maybe not as big of an offense,

00:49:09.040 --> 00:49:11.780
but where the enemies are just kind of spawning

00:49:11.780 --> 00:49:12.900
randomly all over the place.

00:49:12.940 --> 00:49:14.240
They don't really give you a lot of time

00:49:14.240 --> 00:49:16.040
to plan what you're going to do with the claw

00:49:16.040 --> 00:49:17.780
or how you're going to traverse around.

00:49:17.900 --> 00:49:20.200
You just kind of have to go.

00:49:20.740 --> 00:49:21.940
You know, you just have to kind of figure it out.

00:49:22.220 --> 00:49:26.120
So the grappling hook is what, for me,

00:49:26.220 --> 00:49:28.980
is what hurts it, but it's also kind of what saves it.

00:49:29.100 --> 00:49:31.360
Because as flawed as it is,

00:49:31.540 --> 00:49:35.560
I do think that it's worth playing it

00:49:35.560 --> 00:49:38.520
because there's really not been another experience like it.

00:49:39.700 --> 00:49:42.860
And now I am kind of saying the opposite again

00:49:42.860 --> 00:49:43.700
of what you said, Mike,

00:49:43.700 --> 00:49:46.900
where I am sort of saying this just barely makes

00:49:46.900 --> 00:49:47.960
my essential games list.

00:49:48.100 --> 00:49:50.720
And I do sort of suspect that in the future

00:49:50.720 --> 00:49:52.660
I might vote to take it off

00:49:52.660 --> 00:49:54.400
or suggest we take it off.

00:49:54.440 --> 00:49:56.520
But right now I do think that

00:49:56.520 --> 00:49:58.040
with what's on there right now,

00:49:58.900 --> 00:50:00.820
I think it deserves to be on there,

00:50:00.840 --> 00:50:03.040
but I'd like to reassess

00:50:03.040 --> 00:50:04.680
after we've played a lot more games

00:50:04.680 --> 00:50:07.300
and when we get to later ones,

00:50:07.360 --> 00:50:08.440
and we'll see where it is then.

00:50:08.540 --> 00:50:11.700
But this was maybe the hardest decision

00:50:11.700 --> 00:50:13.180
that I've made on the essential games list.

00:50:13.320 --> 00:50:15.060
So I'll put it on there for now,

00:50:15.200 --> 00:50:16.100
but we'll see.

00:50:17.860 --> 00:50:20.340
It's on there anyway. Yeah, no, I love it.

00:50:20.560 --> 00:50:23.440
It's four very interesting votes here.

00:50:24.020 --> 00:50:25.140
You know, this was definitely,

00:50:25.400 --> 00:50:26.920
even though it became unanimous

00:50:26.920 --> 00:50:27.920
on the essential games list,

00:50:27.940 --> 00:50:30.300
it's not the same as Super Mario Brothers

00:50:30.300 --> 00:50:31.700
when that became unanimous

00:50:31.700 --> 00:50:32.600
or The Legend of Zelda.

00:50:33.540 --> 00:50:35.180
Sorry, I know I've already taken up so much time.

00:50:35.280 --> 00:50:36.260
Can I speak to that too?

00:50:36.920 --> 00:50:38.700
Part of me, I don't know how you guys feel about this,

00:50:38.700 --> 00:50:40.680
but after you three had all voted essential,

00:50:41.040 --> 00:50:42.360
I almost wanted to change my vote

00:50:42.360 --> 00:50:45.320
to not essential because I felt like I'm so on the edge

00:50:45.320 --> 00:50:46.920
that I feel like, how can we now have this

00:50:46.920 --> 00:50:48.320
unanimous essential game?

00:50:48.680 --> 00:50:50.200
But I feel like we're going to,

00:50:50.300 --> 00:50:51.580
we'll go with the individual votes

00:50:51.580 --> 00:50:55.020
and not try to influence the overall thing.

00:50:55.280 --> 00:50:56.240
For sure, for sure.

00:50:56.500 --> 00:50:58.880
And there's a lot to be said

00:50:58.880 --> 00:51:00.380
about the essential games list right now.

00:51:00.540 --> 00:51:01.600
It's been a long year.

00:51:02.260 --> 00:51:05.400
1988 has been our longest year of gaming yet,

00:51:05.400 --> 00:51:07.040
and we haven't had a chance

00:51:07.040 --> 00:51:09.020
to really look at the essential games list.

00:51:09.160 --> 00:51:13.140
Honestly, I think it's at 16 or 17 games now,

00:51:13.620 --> 00:51:15.660
and that's not really that large,

00:51:15.700 --> 00:51:17.140
but to me that feels large.

00:51:17.300 --> 00:51:20.360
It feels large to be recommending 17 games

00:51:20.360 --> 00:51:21.760
for people to play. That's a solid collection of games.

00:51:21.760 --> 00:51:25.140
Like, yeah. So it does need a look,

00:51:25.160 --> 00:51:27.860
and we will do that in our Best of 88 episode.

00:51:28.640 --> 00:51:29.560
But, you know,

00:51:29.740 --> 00:51:31.760
everything that's made it on the list so far

00:51:31.760 --> 00:51:36.340
are also games that I was happy to see on there.

00:51:36.540 --> 00:51:40.060
You know, I think now that I'm saying that sentence,

00:51:40.060 --> 00:51:43.320
I'm remembering one that I was a little surprised at,

00:51:43.440 --> 00:51:44.420
but for the most part,

00:51:44.560 --> 00:51:45.960
I was happy to see those games

00:51:45.960 --> 00:51:47.000
on the essential games list.

00:51:47.240 --> 00:51:52.800
Shut your mouth. Anyway, that's been this episode of Nostalgia.

00:51:53.100 --> 00:51:54.500
We hope everybody enjoyed it.

00:51:54.980 --> 00:51:56.760
Bionic Commando, definitely a game

00:51:56.760 --> 00:51:58.840
that probably most of our listeners are familiar with,

00:51:58.840 --> 00:52:01.180
so hopefully you guys made it all the way through the episode

00:52:01.180 --> 00:52:03.360
and argued with us the entire time.

00:52:03.500 --> 00:52:05.220
We love people who argue with us.

00:52:05.360 --> 00:52:08.020
Write on Twitter and tell us how crazy wrong we are,

00:52:08.100 --> 00:52:10.440
and that, actually, you idiots,

00:52:10.660 --> 00:52:12.380
it's easy to save in this game.

00:52:14.360 --> 00:52:16.500
and you save. Like, just say that to us.

00:52:16.500 --> 00:52:20.100
It's fine. I think it was one episode, Sean,

00:52:20.500 --> 00:52:23.040
you and me agreed that Ninja Gaiden,

00:52:23.240 --> 00:52:24.900
or Gaiden, however you want to call it,

00:52:25.220 --> 00:52:27.620
is a one-hit KO game,

00:52:27.620 --> 00:52:28.500
and that's just not true.

00:52:28.700 --> 00:52:32.540
But I said to the person who wrote back to us on Twitter,

00:52:32.660 --> 00:52:34.140
I was like, thank you for letting us know that,

00:52:34.200 --> 00:52:35.740
but also, like, that proves our point

00:52:35.740 --> 00:52:37.700
that we are fresh on these games.

00:52:37.880 --> 00:52:39.860
We never played these games beforehand,

00:52:39.860 --> 00:52:42.160
so you know when you dive into these episodes,

00:52:42.180 --> 00:52:43.000
you're playing with people

00:52:43.000 --> 00:52:44.540
who have no idea what they're talking about

00:52:44.540 --> 00:52:47.180
except for the minute that they start speaking.

00:52:47.560 --> 00:52:49.100
Yeah, and I'll just say that.

00:52:49.240 --> 00:52:50.740
Like, don't speak for me ever again.

00:52:50.960 --> 00:52:54.080
I stand by the fact that it is a one-hit KO game,

00:52:54.220 --> 00:52:55.660
whether or not I've played it or not.

00:52:56.160 --> 00:52:57.320
So, yeah.

00:52:58.040 --> 00:52:59.520
Wow. You're going to have to get on Twitter

00:52:59.520 --> 00:53:01.280
with controversial opinions like that.

00:53:01.540 --> 00:53:03.240
Anyway. Slide into those DMs.

00:53:03.780 --> 00:53:05.040
This has been NostalgiaCast.

00:53:05.120 --> 00:53:06.260
Remember, you can always find us on Twitter

00:53:06.260 --> 00:53:07.780
at NostalgiaCast.

00:53:07.900 --> 00:53:10.920
Next week, we have Blades of Steel coming up.

00:53:11.120 --> 00:53:13.460
No, it is not a Ninja Gaiden game.

00:53:13.460 --> 00:53:14.900
It is a hockey game.

00:53:15.320 --> 00:53:17.760
There are no swords in this one,

00:53:17.940 --> 00:53:19.780
but, you know, Blades of Steel.

00:53:20.060 --> 00:53:20.920
Sean, is that something?

00:53:21.240 --> 00:53:23.380
Like, is that a hockey term for sticks?

00:53:24.420 --> 00:53:27.640
I think at the very least it's the skates.

00:53:28.500 --> 00:53:31.540
I would love to see a game of hockey played

00:53:31.540 --> 00:53:33.040
with steel sticks.

00:53:34.180 --> 00:53:35.740
Like bladed steel sticks.

00:53:36.140 --> 00:53:37.200
Yes, with sights.

00:53:37.460 --> 00:53:39.980
Right, exactly. The Castlevania port over.

00:53:40.900 --> 00:53:43.800
You know, to be fair to everybody involved,

00:53:44.660 --> 00:53:47.460
Blades of Steel is going to get just as fair a shot

00:53:47.460 --> 00:53:49.880
next week as Bionic Commando got today.

00:53:50.040 --> 00:53:51.520
So please tune into that episode.

00:53:51.680 --> 00:53:52.720
I'm sure you'll love it.

00:53:52.720 --> 00:53:55.420
I'm sure you'll love the other 140 episodes

00:53:55.420 --> 00:53:56.380
we've produced so far,

00:53:56.580 --> 00:53:58.600
and I'm sure you'll love the next 600 as well.

